      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Maybe the scenario is when the hypervisor executes the instruction right before wrmsrq, NMI is fired on this CPU. Then the RIP saved in pt_regs points to the wrmsrq instruction, which results in the fixup to skip the wrmsrq instruction.\n\nYes, thats also my understanding. Probably reword it like:\n```\nIf an NMI is delivered at the instruction boundary immediately before the\nextable-protected wrmsrq, the saved RIP points to wrmsrq. The unconditional\nextable lookup then mistakes the NMI for a WRMSR fault and skips the instruction.\n```",
