      "writtenOn": "2026-07-20T14:32:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah - that\u0027s how I understand it too - when instruction before wrmsrq completes, RIP is switched to wrmsrq already but the wrmsrq instruction itself hasn\u0027t executed yet. If a NMI arrives at that moment, pt_regs RIP points to wrmsrq which is why its extable entry gets found and applied, skipping the wrmsr before it ever runs.\n\nI\u0027ve updated the commit log a bit differently. Please let me know if it is better now.",
      "parentUuid": "8d0f0065_0425f2e3",
